From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-ipq6018: enable the PLL across the crypto
 RCG switch

nss_crypto_clk_src selects between the reference oscillator and the
crypto PLL. A root clock generator latches a new source only while that
source is running: the hardware copies the source select on CMD_UPDATE
and reports completion by clearing the bit, which never happens if the
incoming clock is not toggling.

A device tree that assigns this clock a rate served by the PLL performs
the switch from of_clk_set_defaults(), which runs at provider
registration, long before any consumer prepares the branch and with it
the PLL. The update then never completes and the clock stays on the
reference oscillator.

Set CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE so the framework holds the incoming parent
enabled for the duration of the switch, which is what the flag exists
for and what the other qcom generators in this situation carry.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
Index: linux-6.18.44/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
===================================================================
--- linux-6.18.44.orig/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
+++ linux-6.18.44/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq6018.c
@@ -971,6 +971,12 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 nss_crypto_clk_sr
 		.name = "nss_crypto_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = gcc_xo_nss_crypto_pll_gpll0,
 		.num_parents = 3,
+		/*
+		 * A device tree assigned rate switches this to the crypto
+		 * PLL from of_clk_set_defaults(), before any consumer has
+		 * enabled the branch and with it the PLL.
+		 */
+		.flags = CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
 	},
 };
